      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nNext slice of #61024's \"Migrate speculative model code to Flat Model\" bullet (RFC #44219). Moves the HY V3 model and its MTP drafter from the legacy `vllm/model_executor/models/` layout into the new `vllm/models/<name>/<hw>/` layout.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Moves `vllm/model_executor/models/hy_v3.py` and `hy_v3_mtp.py` to `vllm/models/hy_v3/common/{model,mtp}.py`, repointing the `HYV3ForCausalLM` and `HYV3MTPModel` registry entries to `vllm.models.hy_v3`.\n- No logic change. The only diff inside the moved files is fixing imports that crossed the old package boundary (`.utils`, `.interfaces` → `vllm.model_executor.models.{utils,interfaces}`, and the MTP file's `from .hy_v3 import HYV3DecoderLayer` → `from .model import HYV3DecoderLayer`), verified by diffing old vs. new file content.\n- HY V3 needs only a `common/` directory, no `nvidia`/`amd`/`cpu`/`xpu` split: zero custom kernels, and zero platform-conditional code (`grep -c \"is_rocm\\|is_cuda\\|sm90\\|sm100\"` → 0). HY V4 (`vllm.models.hy_v4`), by contrast, needed a real `nvidia`/`amd` split for `flashmla_sparse`/`triton_ihc` -- V3 predates those optimizations.\n- Unlike every other remaining legacy drafter, `hy_v3.py`/`hy_v3_mtp.py` have zero dependency on any other model file -- confirmed by grep across the whole tree, they're the only two files that reference each other. That made this pair the next candidate after Medusa.\n\n## Validation\n\n```\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/models/test_registry.py -q -k HYV3\n# 2 passed\n\npre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py vllm/models/hy_v3/__init__.py vllm/models/hy_v3/common/__init__.py vllm/models/hy_v3/common/model.py vllm/models/hy_v3/common/mtp.py\n# all hooks passed (ruff check/format, mypy, SPDX headers, etc.)\n```\n\nNo e2e acceptance-rate test exists for HY V3 under `tests/v1/e2e/spec_decode/acceptance_rates/` (unlike Medusa, which had one) and I don't have a validated local checkpoint-loading path for it on this change, so the above is the available coverage. `tests/models/registry.py` lists `tencent/Hy3-preview` as the example checkpoint if a reviewer wants to validate a real weight load.\n\n## Details\n\n**Why HY V3 and not another drafter:** every remaining legacy drafter (EAGLE/EAGLE3 variants, the other MTP variants, DFlash) imports its base model's decoder-layer class directly from a still-legacy file (`llama`, `qwen2`, `qwen3`, `deepseek_v2`, etc.), so migrating any of them means migrating a shared, heavily-reused base model too -- a much bigger, higher-blast-radius change. HY V3 is the one pair with zero such entanglement.\n\n**Previous attempt:** #61357 targeted Medusa as the first migration in this series, but Medusa was removed from vLLM entirely in #61701 while that PR was in flight (\"Medusa is not supported by Model Runner V2, and EAGLE/MTP/DFlash/DSpark cover its use case\"). Closed #61357 as superseded by that removal rather than resurrect deleted code.\n\n**Duplicate-work check:** searched open issues/PRs for existing HY V3 Flat Model migration work; found none.\n\n**Scope:** this PR only moves HY V3 + its MTP drafter. The remaining legacy drafters are out of scope here and need their base model migrated alongside them, which is a larger, separate decision per model family.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01S7agbtPNuVe9pxACkqbitP\n",
